{ Calculate a small tree accurately before trying a long line. At every check, test three responses: capture the checker, block the line, or move the king. } 1. Re8+ Rxe8 2. Rxe8# { Illustrative line. The rook on e2 plays Re8+. Black cannot run to f8 or h8 because the rook attacks those squares; its own pawns occupy the escape squares below. There is no interposition available. ...Rxe8 is the only legal reply. Now the e1-rook follows with Rxe8#. Capturing the first checking rook removed Black's last defender. Stop and prove mate by checking every king destination, capture and block, rather than assuming the familiar back-rank pattern is enough. } 1-0

