{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 1. Re8+ Rxe8 2. Rxe8+ Kh7 { Illustrative line. The pawn on h6 leaves h7 empty. Unlike the seventh-rank squares occupied by pawns in Model A, h7 can be a legal king destination. Re8+ Rxe8 Rxe8+ is check, but Black has ...Kh7. The rook on e8 attacks the eighth rank, not h7. A plus sign is correct; a mate sign is not. White began with two rooks against one and finishes with one rook against none. That is a winning material advantage in this simple position, but it still requires conversion. The calculation must report that result accurately instead of calling it mate. } *

