{ A recapture is a candidate, not an obligation. An in-between move can be stronger when it gives check and forces the opponent to answer before recovering material. } 1... Rxc1+ ( 1... exd5 { Alternative for comparison; read the explanation before treating it as a recommendation. } 2. Rxc8# ) 2. Kh2 exd5 { Illustrative line. Black first plays ...Rxc1+. White must answer the check and cannot save the knight at the same time. After Kh2, ...exd5 collects the knight as well. Put the check before the pawn capture. Count the full sequence: Black captures a rook and then a knight while keeping its own rook. Reversing the order is disastrous because White's rook gains access to Black's unprotected back rank. Move order is the entire tactic. } *

